ainer\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"H equals, 1 plus the fraction V sub B over V sub P\"></span></span></p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p><span><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"H equals, V sub B, minus V sub P\"></span></span></p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"a","rationale":"<p>Choice A is correct. The hematocrit can be expressed in terms of the blood volume and the plasma volume by solving the given equation <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"V sub B equals, the fraction with numerator V sub P, and denominator 1 minus H, end fraction\"></span> for <span class=\"italic\">H. </span>Multiplying both sides of this equation by <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"open parenthesis, 1 minus H, close parenthesis \"></span> yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"V sub B, times, open parenthesis, 1 minus H, close parenthesis, equals V sub P\"></span>. Dividing both sides by <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"V sub B \"></span> yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"1 minus H equals, the fraction V sub P, over V sub B\"></span>. Subtracting 1 from both sides yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"negative H equals, negative 1 plus, the fraction V sub P over V sub B\"></span>. Dividing both sides by <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,iVBOR