<p style="text-align: left;">The graphs of the equations in the given system of equations intersect at the point <math alttext="left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> in the <em>xy</em>-plane. What is the value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"57d24b47-79dc-4e70-a4bb-756c8cdf5266","content":"<p><math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"a17c3b30-8bc5-4267-8f0f-39cd4e458287","content":"<p><math alttext=\"24\"><mn>24</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"9ccb14d8-6f95-43f5-b321-ce684182c622","content":"<p><math alttext=\"64\"><mn>64</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"422300ff-644b-4e64-8de4-513b2b31d86f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"72\"><mn>72</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["422300ff-644b-4e64-8de4-513b2b31d86f"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is correct. Since the graphs of the equations in the given system intersect at the point <math alttext="left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, the point <math alttext="left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;represents a solution to the given system of equations. The first equation of the given system of equations states that <math alttext="x equals 8"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>8</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Substituting <math alttext="8"><mn>8</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> in the second equation of the given system of equations yields <math alttext="y equals 8 squared plus 8"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>8</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></math>, or <math alttext="y equals 72"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>72</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, the value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="72"><mn>72</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math>, not <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math>.</p>
<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
