<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction w minus t Over 6 t w EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p>"},{"id":"73f2dff9-0050-4ddc-80ad-739735a8f74d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 6 t w Over w minus t EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. Adding <math alttext=\"StartFraction 2 Over t EndFraction\"><mrow>\n<mfrac>\n<mn>2</mn>\n<mi>t</mi>\n</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</math> to each side of the given equation yields&nbsp;<math alttext=\"StartFraction 12 Over n EndFraction equals minus StartFraction 2 Over w EndFraction plus StartFraction 2 Over t EndFraction\"><mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mfrac>\n<mn>12</mn>\n<mi>n</mi>\n</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mo>-</mo>\n<mfrac>\n<mn>2</mn>\n<mi>w</mi>\n</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n<mo>+</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mfrac>\n<mn>2</mn>\n<mi>t</mi>\n</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. The fractions on the right side of this equation have a common denominator of <math alttext=\"t w\"><mrow>\n<mi>t</mi>\n<mi>w</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>; therefore, the equation can be written as <math alttext=\"StartFraction 12 Over n EndFraction equals StartFraction 2 w Over t w EndFraction minus StartFraction 2 t Over t w EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>w</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext=\"StartFraction 12 Over n EndFraction equals StartFraction 2 w minus 2 t Over t w EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>w</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>, which is equivalent to <math alttext=\"StartFraction 12 Over n EndFraction equals StartFraction 2 left parenthesis w minus t right parenthesis Over t w EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>. Dividing each side of this equation by <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> yields&nbsp;<math alttext=\"StartFraction 6 Over n EndFraction equals StartFraction w minus t Over t w EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>. Since <math alttext=\"n\"><mi>n</mi>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"w minus t\"><mi>w</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi></math> are all positive quantities, taking the reciprocal of each side of the equation <math alttext=\"StartFraction 6 Over n EndFraction equals StartFraction w minus t Over t w EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> yields an equivalent equation: <math alttext=\"StartFraction n Over 6 EndFraction equals StartFraction t w Over w minus t EndFraction\"><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> yields&nbsp;<math alttext=\"n equals StartFraction 6 t w Over w minus t EndFraction\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. This is equivalent to <math alttext=\"StartFraction 1 Over n EndFraction\"><mfrac>\n<mn>1</mn>\n<mi>n</mi>\n</mfrac>\n</math> rather than <math alttext=\"n\"><mi>n</mi>\n</math>.</p>","externalid":"3a6913de-0959-40fb-980c-a37f8b9ee578","correct_answer":["D"]},"createDate":1743430554981,"updateDate":1743430554981}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1743430554981, 1743430554981),
    ($SATQ$c9417793$SATQ$, $SATQ$b40bb858-a515-41ac-963c-90f9040a57b8$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables $SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: center;"><math alttext="StartAbsoluteValue x minus 9 EndAbsoluteValue plus 45 equals 63"><mrow>
