<p style="text-align: left;">What is the sum of the solutions to the given equation?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["18"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["18"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The correct answer is <math alttext="18"><mn>18</mn>
</math>. Subtracting <math alttext="45"><mn>45</mn>
</math> from each side of the given equation yields <math alttext="StartAbsoluteValue x minus 9 EndAbsoluteValue equals 18"><mfenced open="|" close="|"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn></math>. By the definition of absolute value, if <math alttext="StartAbsoluteValue x minus 9 EndAbsoluteValue equals 18"><mfenced open="|" close="|"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn></math>, then <math alttext="x minus 9 equals 18"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mi>x</mi>
		<mo>-</mo>
		<mn>9</mn>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>18</mn>
</mrow>
</math> or <math alttext="x minus 9 equals negative 18"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mi>x</mi>
		<mo>-</mo>
		<mn>9</mn>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Adding <math alttext="9"><mn>9</mn>
</math> to each side of the equation <math alttext="x minus 9 equals 18"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mi>x</mi>
		<mo>-</mo>
		<mn>9</mn>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>18</mn>
</mrow>
</math> yields <math alttext="x equals 27"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>27</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Adding <math alttext="9"><mn>9</mn>
</math> to each side of the equation <math alttext="x minus 9 equals negative 18"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mi>x</mi>
		<mo>-</mo>
		<mn>9</mn>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn>
</mrow>
</math> yields <math alttext="x equals negative 9"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, the solutions to the given equation are <math alttext="27"><mn>27</mn>
</math> and <math alttext="negative 9"><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn>
</math>, and it follows that the sum of the solutions to the given equation is <math alttext="27 plus left parenthesis negative 9 right parenthesis"><mn>27</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext="18"><mn>18</mn>
</math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"c9417793","external_id":"b40bb858-a515-41ac-963c-90f9040a57b8","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"87b4c941-4a7d-4a56-8ee1-83e76a71b41c","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.B.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables ","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"StartAbsoluteValue x minus 9 EndAbsoluteValue plus 45 equals 63\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\">\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>9</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>45</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>63</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">What is the sum of the solutions to the given equation?</p>","answerOptions":[],"keys":["18"],"correct_answer":["18"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"18\"><mn>18</mn>\n</math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"45\"><mn>45</mn>\n</math> from each side of the given equation yields <math alttext=\"StartAbsoluteValue x minus 9 EndAbsoluteValue equals 18\"><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn></math>. By the definition of absolute value, if <math alttext=\"StartAbsoluteValue x minus 9 EndAbsoluteValue equals 18\"><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn></math>, then <math alttext=\"x minus 9 equals 18\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>9</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>18</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> or <math alttext=\"x minus 9 equals negative 18\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>-<