<p style="text-align: left;">The graph of&nbsp;<math alttext="y equals g left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is shown. If <math alttext="g left parenthesis x plus 28 right parenthesis equals one tenth left parenthesis x minus a right parenthesis squared left parenthesis x minus b right parenthesis squared left parenthesis x minus c right parenthesis"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>28</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, where <math alttext="a"><mi>a</mi>
</math>, <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math>, and <math alttext="c"><mi>c</mi>
</math> are constants, which of the following could be the value of <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"ea98cf83-be13-44f7-a61b-31bd051ada32","content":"<p><math alttext=\"31\"><mn>31</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"b1184a04-aba5-44f1-85b8-85fa4820f436","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"243d7df8-784a-4ea3-a19c-b523db9cdc99","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 2\"><mrow>\n\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t<mn>2</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"28776a48-c384-4619-b0fc-165bd15c33e8","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 25\"><mrow>\n\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t<mn>25</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["28776a48-c384-4619-b0fc-165bd15c33e8"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is correct. Substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b"><mi>b</mi></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> in the given equation yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis b plus 28 right parenthesis equals one tenth left parenthesis b minus a right parenthesis squared left parenthesis b minus b right parenthesis squared left parenthesis b minus c right parenthesis"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, which is equivalent to <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis b plus 28 right parenthesis equals one tenth left parenthesis b minus a right parenthesis squared left parenthesis 0 right parenthesis squared left parenthesis b minus c right parenthesis"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis b plus 28 right parenthesis equals 0"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. It follows that when <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x equals b plus 28"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>28</mn></math>, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 0"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. There are three points where the graph of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals g left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> intersects the <em>x</em>-axis: <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis negative 2 comma 0 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis 1 comma 0 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis 3 comma 0 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis negative 2 right parenthesis equals 0"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis 1 right parenthesis equals 0"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis 3 right parenthesis equals 0"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. It follows that either <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b plus 28 equals negative 2"><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b plus 28 equals 1"><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b plus 28 equals 3"><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. Subtracting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="28"><mn>28</mn></math> from each side of the equation <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b plus 28 equals negative 2"><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math> yields&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b equals negative 30"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>30</mn></math>. Subtracting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="28"><mn>28</mn></math> from each side of the equation <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b plus 28 equals 1"><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> yields&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b equals negative 27"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>27</mn></math>. Subtracting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="28"><mn>28</mn></math> from each side of the equation <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b plus 28 equals 3"><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math> yields&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b equals negative 25"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>25</mn></math>. Thus, the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b"><mi>b</mi></math> must be either&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="negative 30"><mo>-</mo><mn>30</mn></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="negative 27"><mo>-</mo><mn>27</mn></math>, or&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="negative 25"><mo>-</mo><mn>25</mn></math>. Of these values, only&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="negative 25"><mo>-</mo><mn>25</mn></math> is given as a choice.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This would be a possible value of&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b"><mi>b</mi></math> if the graph shown was the graph of&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals g left parenthesis x plus 28 right parenthesis"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, not&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals g left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. This would be the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="c"><mi>c</mi></math>, not the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b"><mi>b</mi></math>, if the graph shown was the graph of&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals g left parenthesis x plus 28 right parenthesis"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, not&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals g left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"c946d5bd","external_id":"f4d42535-f2e1-455c-b197-383e00a2a878","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"54ef51e7-a73d-4e89-9cdf-da9151419de8","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.C.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg version=\"1.0.0\" width=\"370px\" height=\"361.328125px\" viewBox=\"0 0 370 361.328125\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-label=\"Graph of a curve in the x y plane with the origin labeled O. The x axis ranges from negative 5 to 5. The y axis ranges from negative 10 to 10. Refer to long description.\"><defs><marker id=\"arrow\" viewBox=\"0 -3 10 6\" markerUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\" markerWidth=\"10px\" markerHeight=\"6px\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,-3 L10,0 L0,3\" fill=\"currentColor\"></path></marker></defs><g class=\"graph-group\" transform=\"translate(0, 25)\"><g class=\"grid-group\"><g class=\"x-grid\"><line x1=\"168.6640625\" y1=\"336.328125\" x2=\"168.6640625\" y2=\"0\" str