$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<span class=\"math_expression \">\n            <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/cc776a04/img_000_f76ec652.png\" alt=\"negative 2 point 2, x squared, plus 1 point 6\"></span>\n          </span>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<span class=\"math_expression \">\n            <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/cc776a04/img_001_d7452e24.png\" alt=\"negative 2 point 2, x squared, plus 11 point 2\"></span>\n          </span>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<span class=\"math_expression \">\n            <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/cc776a04/img_002_c89a726b.png\" alt=\"negative 2 point 95, x squared, minus 7 point 2 x, plus 12 point 16\"></span>\n          </span>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<span class=\"math_expression \">\n            <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/cc776a04/img_003_008be088.png\" alt=\"negative 2 point 95, x squared, minus 7 point 2 x, plus 0 point 64\"></span>\n          </span>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is correct. The first expression <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/cc776a04/img_005_f02b9a56.png" alt="open parenthesis, 1 point 5 x minus 2 point 4, close parenthesis, squared"></span> can be rewritten as <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/cc776a04/img_006_fafd92d8.png" alt="open parenthesis, 1 point 5 x minus 2 point 4, close parenthesis, times, open parenthesis, 1 point 5 x minus 2 point 4, close parenthesis"></span> . Applying the distributive property to this product yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/cc776a04/img_007_5a16f0b9.png" alt="open parenthesis, 2 point 2 5, x squared, minus 3 point 6 x, minus 3 point 6 x, plus 5 point 7 6, close parenthesis, minus, open parenthesis, 5 point 2, x squared, minus 6 point 4, close parenthesis"></span> . This difference can be rewritten as <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/cc776a04/img_008_4e6bc4c6.png" alt="open parenthesis, 2 point 2 5, x squared, minus 3 point 6 x, minus 3 point 6 x, plus 5 point 7 6, close parenthesis, plus, negative 1 times, open parenthesis, 5 point 2 x squared, minus 6 point 4, close parenthesis"></span> . Distributing the factor of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/cc776a04/img_009_d3b569af.png" alt="negative 1"></span> through the second expression yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/cc776a04/img_010_1ce9e443.png" alt="2 point 2 5 x, squared, minus 3 point 6 x, minus 3 point 6 x, plus 5 point 7 6, minus 5 point 2, x squared, plus 6 point 4"></span> . Regrouping like terms, the expression becomes <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/cc776a04/img_011_17ba4e74.png" alt="open parenthesis, 2 point 2 5, x squared, minus 5 point 2, x squared, close parenthesis, plus, open parenthesis, negative 3 point 6 x minus 3 point 6 x, close parenthesis, plus, open parenthesis, 5 point 7 6 plus 6 point 4, close parenthesis"></span> . Combining like terms yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/cc776a04/img_012_4c6a78c0.png" alt="negative 2 point 9 5, x squared, minus 7 point 2 x, plus 12 point 1 6"></span> .<p>Choices A, B, and D are incorrect and likely result from errors made when applying the distributive property or combining the resulting like terms.</p></p>
